.TH GIT-WORKFLOW-ALIASES 1 2026-10-03 git-workflow "git-workflow manual"
.SH NAME
git-workflow-aliases \- set up, list, reset or remove the git-workflow aliases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git workflow aliases
.RB [ list ]
.br
.B git workflow aliases install
.RI [ set ...]
.br
.B git workflow aliases reset
.IR set ...
.br
.B git workflow aliases remove
.RI [ set ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
An alias set is a git config file of aliases. There are two:
.TP
.B commands
Short names for the commands, the names they had in 1.x:
.BR "b = workflow branch" ,
.BR "c = workflow commit" ,
.BR qc ,
.BR ps ,
.BR sq ,
.B sync
and
.BR rb\-pull ,
plus
.B wf = workflow
for everything else.
.TP
.B extras
General-purpose aliases:
.BR lg ,
.BR graph ,
.BR s ,
.BR st ,
.BR aa ,
.B au
and
.BR fprune .
.PP
The defaults ship with git-workflow. Your copies live in
.I ~/.config/git\-workflow/aliases/
and are included from
.IR ~/.gitconfig ,
so you can edit them like any other git config file. A copy under your home
directory is included as
.IR ~/.config/... ,
not by its full path, so a
.I ~/.gitconfig
you sync between machines works on each.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install \fR[\fIset\fR...]
Copy each set (default:
.BR commands )
to your config directory, unless a copy is already there, and include it from
.IR ~/.gitconfig .
An existing copy is never overwritten. An alias you already define, in
.I ~/.gitconfig
or a file it includes, is left out of the new copy (commented out, with a
note), so yours keeps working. It warns when a
.BI git\- name
program on
.B PATH
would run instead of an alias, as git prefers programs to aliases. It
removes a 1.x include of the old alias file; when there was one and no
.I set
is named, it installs
.B extras
as well, since the 1.x file had them.
.TP
.B reset \fIset\fR...
Replace your copy with the default, keeping yours as
.IR set .bak.
.TP
.B remove \fR[\fIset\fR...]
Stop including each set (default: all of them). Your copies stay.
.TP
.B list
The default. Show each alias that runs a git-workflow command, and where each
set is and whether it is included.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/git\-workflow/aliases/
Your copies;
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
replaces
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.I <prefix>/share/git\-workflow/aliases/
The defaults.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-workflow (1),
.BR git\-config (1)
